  "artifacts": [
    {
      "type": "conversation",
      "label": "how accurate is this branch?",
      "uri": "{\"version\":1,\"sessionId\":\"148bbd31-97a4-4aea-ab44-0c137b510e0d\",\"title\":\"how accurate is this branch?\",\"capturedAt\":1783429355875,\"turns\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"how accurate is this branch?\",\"timestamp\":1783426099200,\"selection\":[{\"actionHash\":\"uhCkkShk1I0NAUKkYkWzeksxWWYJhoqqDNpgJUVtWT9dE6s4I4yR4\",\"id\":\"161039\",\"content\":\"Completion criteria attached at any node level determine that node's achievement\"}]},{\"role\":\"agent\",\"content\":\"⚙ Terminal (pending)I audited the branch against the live code (computedState.ts, awaitingEval.ts, outcomeFields.ts, CompletionCriteriaField.tsx). Overall verdict: **largely accurate, with two tasks now stale-unchecked** because newer code (commit 3c88d7aa's regression/signoff colours) overtook them.\\n\\n**Node-by-node:**\\n\\n- **[[completion]] (branch)** — accurate as a target-state. The core claim \\\"achievement is the consequence of criteria\\\" is still *not* realized: `computeAchievementStatus` never reads `completionCriteria`, and lines 79–86 explicitly let a manual `Achieved` flag override everything. The branch being all-NotAchieved matches reality.\\n- **\\\"Every criterion names an evaluator\\\" (2/4)** — accurate. Schema `{statement, evaluator, evidence?, met?, by?, at?}` and the human stamp widget exist; no executable runner, no LLM path (the widget's own comment confirms verdicts are hand-recorded).\\n- **\\\"Leaf Achieved as recorded consequence\\\" (0/3)** — accurate. The bare toggle still rules. Nuance: the *gap* is now visible (`isReadyForSignoff` gold state = \\\"all criteria met but not yet Achieved\\\"), but derivation isn't built.\\n- **\\\"Small's achievement from tasks+criteria\\\" (0/3)** — accurate on the substance. Minor: task 1 (\\\"surface the task list as editable todos\\\") describes something Acorn has always had — arguably pre-satisfied.\\n- **\\\"Branch integration criteria\\\" (0/3)** — **partly stale.** Task 3 (\\\"flag all-children-achieved-but-criterion-fails\\\") is essentially built: `hasCriteriaRegression` is deliberately not scope-gated and renders a warning colour on any Achieved node with an unmet criterion. Gating branch achievement itself (task 2) is not built.\\n- **\\\"Executable criteria re-run\\\" (0/3)** — **partly stale.** Task 2 (\\\"newly-failing criterion surfaces red\\\") exists via `hasCriteriaRegression` + `CRITERIA_REGRESSION` colours — though triggered by a verdict flipping, not by an automatic re-run (task 1, not built). Ancestor tinting (task 3): not built.\\n- **\\\"Displays verdicts, roll up\\\" (0/2)** — accurate, slightly understated: criteria *state* already drives three map colours (pink awaiting-eval, gold signoff, red regression), but per-criterion verdicts don't render on the map node and don't feed achievement.\\n- **\\\"Computed results stored separately, drive colour\\\" (1/3)** — accurate; its 2026-07-06 audit note matches the code exactly (in-memory Redux only, colour mapping done, no caching/rollup).\\n\\nWant me to propose a draft checking the two overtaken tasks (with evidence pointing at `awaitingEval.ts` / commit 3c88d7aa) and adding a status note to the branch-criteria node?\",\"timestamp\":1783426099203,\"toolCalls\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01DZNdS5fin6wBVECF87utmX\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01RvwEXCSn6kzTZEHihR4j3N\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_0148cgcbYtMZWwg9nP1biTum\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01X9zXRTbGE2TmYcj1K5RLyV\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01QNwww1zWYk4YTMLNMhk7QV\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"yes\",\"timestamp\":1783426348431,\"selection\":[{\"actionHash\":\"uhCkkZYyvMndVpgXJlqptBoD0SzF2rxqnETGL2qHM3u6JonSS_jiD\",\"id\":\"154739\",\"content\":\"Multiple sessions run turns concurrently in one window, and switching between them never cancels, blocks, or hides a running turn\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"↻ sent updated tree\",\"timestamp\":1783426348434},{\"role\":\"agent\",\"content\":\"⚙ ToolSearch (pending)Draft opened — 2 nodes updated, nothing committed yet:\\n\\n1. **\\\"Branch nodes carry integration-test criteria\\\"** — checked task 3 (*flag all-children-achieved-but-criterion-fails*), added a status note: the flag exists via `hasCriteriaRegression` (not scope-gated, commit 3c88d7aa) + the CRITERIA_REGRESSION warning colour; the achievement *gate* (task 2) is explicitly still open since `computeAchievementStatus` never reads criteria. Attached `awaitingEval.ts` as a workproduct.\\n\\n2. **\\\"Executable criteria re-run\\\"** — checked task 2 (*newly-failing criterion surfaces red*), added a spec note making the caveat explicit: today's trigger is a **verdict flip** (human un-check or agent-posted fail), not an automatic re-run — tasks 1 and 3 (runner, ancestor tinting) stay open, so the \\\"up the branch\\\" criterion stays unmet.\\n\\nOne thing I deliberately left alone: task 1 on the branch-criteria node (\\\"a branch can author its own criteria\\\") is arguably also already true — branches in this very tree carry authored criteria. Say the word if you'd like that checked too; otherwise review and Confirm/reject per node.\",\"timestamp\":1783426348434,\"toolCalls\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_014VeSEdxwGMM68YtsLmdXR8\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01QgBfgKJurAUBdsQz51cSb3\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"}]}],\"agentName\":\"@agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp\"}"
