  "spec": "Computed achievement at a branch = (all children achieved) AND (the branch's own completion criteria pass). Integration criteria are ordinary completion criteria authored at the branch, usually executable.\n\nSTATUS 2026-07-07 (code audit): the FLAG task is built — hasCriteriaRegression (web/src/awaitingEval.ts, commit 3c88d7aa) is deliberately NOT scope-gated ('a branch's own (integration) criteria can regress exactly the way a leaf's can'): any node shown Achieved while a criterion's met flag is not true renders the CRITERIA_REGRESSION warning colour (web/src/styles.ts, argsForDrawBackgroundColor/Border). NOT built: the achievement GATE itself — computeAchievementStatus (web/src/redux/persistent/projects/outcomes/computedState.ts) derives branch achievement purely from children and never reads completionCriteria, so a failing integration criterion warns but does not yet block Achieved propagation (task 2 and this node's executable criterion remain open).",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "A branch with all children achieved but a failing integration criterion is not shown achieved",
      "evaluator": "executable"
    }
