      "uri": "{\"version\":1,\"sessionId\":\"eb1a9d18-a0c0-45d6-b0a6-983d834b3002\",\"title\":\"we should update this node to be more accurate to what wa…\",\"capturedAt\":1782969060863,\"turns\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"we should update this node to be more accurate to what was done.   Also is it elsewhere in the tree?\",\"timestamp\":1782965099034,\"selection\":[{\"actionHash\":\"uhCkkrRi-hTIIKO4rIu-_W84SjrD6GWgPqHjSQyyYHp5-ANQf5AiG\",\"id\":\"486471\",\"content\":\"Agents attach their workproduct to nodes as output artifacts\"}]},{\"role\":\"agent\",\"content\":\"I'll ground this before proposing. Let me look at the actual artifacts UI code and load the Acorn tools in parallel.Let me read the current live tree to ground my proposal.Let me extract the current state of this node and check for duplication via a subagent, keeping the big output out of my context.I have what I need. Here's the picture before I propose.\\n\\n**Is it elsewhere in the tree? — Yes, substantially.** The *mechanism* this node describes (an agent attaching produced outputs onto a node) is already owned by two other nodes:\\n- **`agent-postback`** (`Agents post completion verdicts with evidence back onto the nodes they worked`) — its spec explicitly says the propose_edits write-back *\\\"attaches workproduct artifacts.\\\"*\\n- **the branch-E parent** (`Every node can hold a list of attachments`) — already specifies *\\\"work-product outputs (files, PRs, build logs) that agents produce\\\"* with a `role: output (i.e. work-product)`.\\n- `do-it-trigger` and the root also reference the same \\\"produced artifacts flow back onto the node\\\" arrow.\\n\\nSo this node was largely restating its own parent + agent-postback. And what it claimed as unbuilt is mostly *already working*: I checked the code, and agents attach workproduct artifacts through `propose_edits` today — nearly every built leaf in this tree carries agent-authored `type: \\\"workproduct\\\"` artifacts that render in `ArtifactsField.tsx`. The one thing genuinely **not** built is task 2: the UI does **not** distinguish input artifacts from output/workproduct ones — every non-conversation artifact renders as an identical `type/label/uri` row, and there's no `role` field.\\n\\nSo the accurate move is to narrow this node to its non-duplicated residue (the input↔output presentation) and record that the attach-and-render half is done. Proposing that as a draft:Draft's open for your review (nothing committed). Here's what I changed and the honest choices in it:\\n\\n**Reframed to match reality**\\n- **Outcome** now says the attach-and-render half *already works* — agents propose `workproduct` artifacts via `propose_edits`, you Confirm, they render in `ArtifactsField.tsx` — and names the genuine residue: the UI doesn't distinguish input/clarity artifacts from output/workproduct ones (no `role` field; all rows render identically).\\n- **Tasks**: task 1 (\\\"agent-produced outputs attach via propose_edits and render\\\") → **checked**; task 2 rewritten as the real remaining work (input↔output distinction: a `role` field or visual grouping/badge). The old \\\"Artifact API\\\" task is gone — there's no separate API; it's propose_edits over `fields.artifacts`.\\n- **Criteria**: the existing executable criterion is marked **met** with evidence (this whole tree is the proof). Added a **human** criterion for the input/output visual distinction — unmet. So the node stays **NotAchieved**, correctly, on that one open task.\\n- **Artifacts**: replaced the empty \\\"example PR link\\\" placeholder with the two real files (`ArtifactsField.tsx`, `outcomeFields.ts`).\\n\\n**Is it elsewhere?** Yes — flagged in the new spec: the *mechanism* is owned by **`agent-postback`** (propose_edits write-back \\\"attaches workproduct artifacts\\\") and already specified by the **branch-E parent**. So I scoped this node down to the one thing that's uniquely its own — the output-vs-input presentation.\\n\\nTwo things worth