uhCkknVoG1DvClZIHxrwstm5H45wm5RFg12ax-nK.description:
{"outcome":"When a node's handle appears in rendered text — an outcome/spec markdown field, a completion criterion, a chat message — it renders as a clickable reference, and clicking it brings that node to the centre of the map (selected and framed). A reference isn't just readable, it's navigable: click [[work-loop]] in prose and the map jumps to it.","handle":"handle-link","spec":"In rendered markdown/chat text, detect handle tokens written as [[handle]] (the proposed in-text reference syntax) and render them as links. On click: resolveRef(project, handle) -> actionHash, then dispatch select + centre/zoom-to-node on the map (reuse the existing pan/zoom-to-node action; see branch I's fit-to-changed for the camera move). An unresolved handle renders as plain/dim text, never a broken link. Relies-on resolveRef (built — node-ref-resolver) and the map's centre-on-node capability.

RENDER SITES: RichText is wired into MarkdownDescription (outcome/spec fields), agent chat messages, AND (2026-07-01) user-authored chat messages. The token regex accepts numeric slugs, so a bare [[123456]] hashCodeId is a valid, resolvable reference too — resolveRef maps handle / hashCodeId / actionHash alike.","completionCriteria":[{"statement":"The text-to-links transform detects [[handle]] tokens and resolveRef maps each to its node (or null for unknown); pure + unit-tested","evaluator":"executable","met":true,"at":1782416387970,"evidence":"2026-06-25: PURE transform built + unit-tested. web/src/handleLinks.ts: splitHandleTokens (detect [[handle]] slug tokens), parseHandleLinks(text, resolve) maps each handle to an actionHash via nodeRef.resolveRef or null for unknown, and remarkHandleLinks (mdast plugin) rewrites [[handle]] text into link nodes (skipping code spans + existing links). web/test/handleLinks.test.ts: 11 tests pass (detection, multiple/adjacent handles, malformed-bracket rejection, known->actionHash, unknown->null, mdast transform incl. code/link untouched). Full suite 235/235 green; tsc clean on touched files (26 pre-existing node_modules errors unchanged)."},{"statement":"Clicking a handle reference in a node's text (or chat) selects that node and centres/zooms the map on it; an unknown handle is not a broken link","evaluator":"human","met":true,"by":"uhCAkBMyVDKMRR5CqsiZ-K5FQ3ozs27uURhdp48F7Ck56t7o3hyUW","at":1782417146897,"evidence":"2026-06-25 BUILT: web/src/components/RichText/RichText.tsx wraps ReactMarkdown with remarkHandleLinks + a custom anchor + transformLinkUri (allows the handle: scheme past react-markdown URL sanitizing). A resolved [[handle]] renders as a clickable .handle-ref that on click preventDefault+stopPropagation and dispatches animatePanAndZoom(actionHash, true); an unknown handle renders as dim plain text (.handle-ref--unresolved). Wired into MarkdownDescription and HarnessChat (agent messages).

2026-07-01 FIX (Eric found [[192260]] not clickable in his OWN chat message): user/system chat messages had rendered as raw {m.text} — only AGENT messages went through RichText, so handles the human typed were never linkified. FIXED: HarnessChat now renders user messages through RichText too (system notices like '↻ sent updated tree' stay plain). Since the token regex accepts digits and resolveRef handles hashCodeId, a numeric [[192260]] the human types is now a working link. Awaiting Eric live re-verify."}],"artifacts":[{"type":"workproduct","label":"handleLinks.ts — splitHandleTokens / parseHandleLinks / remarkHandleLinks (pure detection + resolution + mdast plugin)","uri":"web/src/handleLinks.ts"},{"type":"workproduct","label":"RichText.tsx — ReactMarkdown wrapper: handle-link anchor, transformLinkUri for the handle: scheme, click -> animatePanAndZoom; null-safe redux read","uri":"web/src/components/RichText/RichText.tsx"},{"type":"workproduct","label":"RichText.scss — .handle-ref / .handle-ref--unresolved styling","uri":"web/src/components/RichText/RichText.scss"},{"type":"workproduct","label":"MarkdownDescription.tsx + HarnessChat.tsx — render outcome/spec fields and chat (BOTH user + agent messages) through RichText","uri":"web/src/components/HarnessChat/HarnessChat.tsx"},{"type":"workproduct","label":"handleLinks.test.ts — 11 tests: token detection + resolveRef mapping + mdast transform","uri":"web/test/handleLinks.test.ts"}]}

