{
  "outcome": "A model running entirely on the local machine — no calls leaving the host — drives the full clarity-tree loop: the in-app chat hands it the tree, it calls read_tree, proposes a well-formed propose_edits ProjectDiff, and the human Confirms it. This is the headline 'fully locally running LLM' example: Acorn's agentic tree-editing works air-gapped. Stack: LFM2.5-8B-A1B (Ollama) driven through the OpenCode ACP agent, all on a no-GPU laptop.",
  "spec": "MODEL: LiquidAI LFM2.5-8B-A1B (GGUF, Q4_K_M ~5.16GB) — a 'lfm2moe' MoE with ~1B ACTIVE params per token, CPU/edge-friendly; Liquid positions it for agentic tool-use. It emits PYTHONIC tool calls between <|tool_call_start|> tokens (its OWN format, not Anthropic Messages), so the claude-agent-acp path (harness:openrouter) is a poor fit; run it under Ollama, whose template parses those tokens into standard tool_calls.\n\nACP AGENT — DECIDED 2026-06-18 (research): OpenCode, launched as a stdio ACP agent with `opencode acp`. Chosen because OpenCode's ACPSessionManager accepts mcpServers passed per-session via ACP session/new — exactly how Acorn's sidecar attaches read_tree/propose_edits (sidecar.js newSession mcpServers) — and it exposes 75+ providers incl. Ollama.\n\nBUILT 2026-06-18: `yarn harness:local` (root package.json) sets OPENCODE_CONFIG=web/dev-harness/opencode.local.json + ACORN_HARNESS_CMD='opencode acp'. opencode.local.json declares provider=ollama (baseURL http://localhost:11434/v1) + model lfm2.5:8b-a1b. dev-harness/README.md documents the stack, the OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH bump, the tiny-project rule, the egress-block check, and the Goose fallback. STILL TO RUN LIVE: pull the model, raise context, and drive the loop on a tiny project.\n\nUPDATE 2026-07-06 (commit 929e1de7 'backend-agnostic prompt delivery + direct OpenAI/Ollama backend'): a SECOND, simpler local route now exists alongside opencode — web/dev-harness/directBackend.js speaks OpenAI chat-completions directly to Ollama/LM Studio (env ACORN_OPENAI_BASE_URL + ACORN_OPENAI_MODEL) and runs its own tool-call loop against the Acorn tools, removing the ACP-agent middleman and its session/new MCP-attachment risk entirely. promptContext.js composes tree context for backends without a system-prompt slot; systemSlot.js seats the system prompt per backend. `yarn harness:ollama` launches it. All three are unit-tested (directBackend.test.ts, promptContext.test.ts, systemSlot.test.ts). The live egress-blocked end-to-end run is STILL PENDING — either route can be the one that proves it.\n\nGoose is the fallback ACP agent (MCP-native, ACP server, Ollama via OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434).\n\nTHREE THINGS TO VERIFY LIVE:\n1. TOOL ATTACHMENT (residual risk, opencode route only): confirm the Acorn MCP tools actually attach via ACP session/new in opencode — there is a reported class of 'session/new MCP servers don't work in ACP mode' bug. Fallback if they don't: register acornToolsServer (already bridges to the sidecar via ACORN_WEB_PORT) directly in opencode.local.json under `mcp`. (The directBackend route sidesteps this entirely.)\n2. CONTEXT: read_tree on THIS project is ~137k chars (~40k tokens); Ollama's default context is 4096 — raise OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH and run the demo against a TINY 3–6 node project.\n3. TOOL TEMPLATE: Ollama issue #15953 reported smaller LFM2.5 builds not accepting tool calls despite supporting them — confirm the 8b-a1b build enables it.\n\nThe binding constraint stays tool-calling fidelity: can LFM2-8B-A1B emit a well-formed propose_edits ProjectDiff for a small tree?",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "With egress to api.anthropic.com (and other model APIs) blocked, an in-app chat message against a SMALL demo project is answered by LFM2.5-8B-A1B on localhost (Ollama) via the opencode ACP agent, which calls read_tree and emits a propose_edits draft the human Confirms — captured with model + host config as evidence",
      "evaluator": "human"
    },
    {
      "statement": "A single documented dev command (yarn harness:local) brings up the local Ollama-backed opencode ACP backend so the example is reproducible",
      "evaluator": "human",
      "evidence": "2026-06-18 BUILT (awaiting Eric's live run): yarn harness:local added to root package.json; web/dev-harness/opencode.local.json (provider=ollama, model lfm2.5:8b-a1b); dev-harness/README.md 'Fully-local LLM' section with the 3-step runbook. The command + config exist; live execution still pending. 2026-07-06: yarn harness:ollama (directBackend.js) is now a second single-command local route."
