{
  "outcome": "A node's typed-artifacts list gains a 'conversation' artifact whose value is a captured transcript and whose widget renders the turns inline as a readable thread, so a retained conversation is legible on the node rather than an opaque link. An empty/placeholder conversation reads as an explicit empty state, not a broken row.",
  "spec": "Extend the typed artifacts (branch E ArtifactsField) with a conversation type/role: it stores or references a transcript (from the capture leaf) and renders each turn (role + content) as a readable thread in the node editor, distinct from the input/output reference artifacts. Relies-on branch E typed artifacts and the transcript shape.\n\nIMPLEMENTED 2026-06-30: the conversation artifact REUSES OutcomeArtifact {type,label,uri} — type='conversation', serialized Transcript carried in `uri`. web/src/harness/conversationArtifact.ts (pure): CONVERSATION_ARTIFACT_TYPE, isConversationArtifact, makeConversationArtifact, conversationTranscript (parses uri; null on malformed). ArtifactsField detects a conversation artifact BY TYPE (not by a successful parse) and renders ConversationArtifact.tsx instead of the type/label/uri row: turns as a thread (You/Agent/System badge + content + thinking + tool-call lines), the ask-time 're:' anchor, and a collapsible plan section. Tinted, left-accented card (OutcomeFieldsEditor.scss).\n\nEMPTY STATE 2026-06-30 (Eric flagged the placeholder on branch-transcript showed nothing): a conversation artifact whose uri is empty or unparseable now renders an explicit 'No transcript captured yet — attach a chat session to fill it in.' card (ConversationArtifact handles transcript=null / zero turns), instead of degrading to a bare editable row. The real transcript is populated by the attach-control sibling.",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "A node carrying a conversation artifact renders its turns as a readable thread in the editor",
