  "spec": "The conversation artifact carries a serialized Transcript in its uri; copies are costly. Three rules: (1) UPSERT/GROW — on attach, if the target already has a conversation artifact with the same transcript.sessionId, replace it in place; otherwise append one. (2) REFERENCE, don't copy — a node discussing a conversation held elsewhere links to the holder via [[handle]], never its own copy. (3) MULTI-NODE GUARD — attaching a session already held on another node warns and attaches a reference by default.\n\nIMPLEMENTED 2026-07-01: web/src/harness/conversationDedup.ts (pure): upsertConversationArtifact (replace-by-sessionId, else append — the canonical copy GROWS, never forks), findConversationHolders (scan the tree for nodes already holding a session), and the conversation-ref artifact (CONVERSATION_REF_TYPE + makeConversationReference / isConversationRef / conversationRefTarget). HarnessChat.submitAttach now: upserts on the chosen node (grow in place); if the session is already held on ANOTHER node it attaches a lightweight [[ref]] to the canonical holder instead of a second copy (with a 'copy anyway' checkbox in the inline picker + a holder note). ArtifactsField renders a conversation-ref as a compact clickable [[ref]] line (via RichText), distinct from the full thread. (Also moved the conversation delete control to the TOP-right of the thread — it was buried mid-stream.)\n\nRelies-on the attach control (sibling), the conversation artifact type (sibling), and the handle-link feature ([[handle]]).",
